  "Cursor marks a unique position or index into the connection."
  cursor: String!
  "The update."
  node: TownsquareUpdate
  "If the update is missing, this tells you why."
  nodeMissingReason: TownsquareConnectedUpdateNodeMissingReason
  "The sub-goal or key result this update came from."
  sourceGoal: TownsquareGoal
  "The project this update came from."
  sourceProject: TownsquareProject
}

"""
Updates from the entities connected to a goal, grouped by the kind of entity they came from.

Every group is ordered by the health of the work behind it, worst first: off track, at risk, on
track, completed, paused, pending, then cancelled. Within one of those tiers the newest update comes
first.

Reached from two places, which read that health from different points in time. On TownsquareGoal the
groups are resolved live, so they show the current state of the connected work and are ordered by
the health of each connected entity right now; an entity that has never been updated is placed by
its own phase and status like any other. On TownsquareGoalUpdate the groups are read back from the
set recorded when that update was published, so they show the state of the work as it stood at the
time it was written and are ordered by the health recorded then - the order of a published update
never changes as the work behind it moves on. An entry whose target cannot be read has no health to
order on and sorts last.
"""
type TownsquareConnectedUpdates @renamed(from : "ConnectedUpdates") {
  "Latest update from each directly linked project."
  projectUpdates(after: String, first: Int): TownsquareConnectedUpdateConnection
  "Latest update from each direct sub-goal that is not a key result."
  subGoalUpdates(after: String, first: Int): TownsquareConnectedUpdateConnection
  "Latest update from each direct key result (a sub-goal whose type kind is SUCCESS_MEASURE)."
  successMeasureUpdates(after: String, first: Int): TownsquareConnectedUpdateConnection
}

