"What running a step does."
enum HypothesisMitigationActionType {
  """
  Pause the rollout of the Switcheroo feature gate the hypothesis blames. Produces no pull request,
  so it reports its own sub-steps.
  """
  PAUSE_FEATURE_FLAG
  """
  Raise a revert of the commit the hypothesis blames, through the merged pull request that carried it.
  Fails when the commit belongs to no merged pull request or to several merged pull requests.
  """
  REVERT_COMMIT
  "Raise a revert of the pull request the hypothesis blames."
  REVERT_PR
}

"""
Confidence classification for a mitigation plan, mirroring MitigationConfidence. Bucketed from the
P90 of the scores of the sources the plan was drawn from, by the same rules as the legacy surface.
"""
enum HypothesisMitigationConfidence {
  HIGH
  LOW
  MEDIUM
}

"""
How a caller wants a plan step executed. Deliberately not HypothesisMitigationActionType: which
action a step runs is fixed by its plan, whereas whether the responder ran it or did the work
themselves is something no server state can reconstruct.
"""
enum HypothesisMitigationExecutionMode {
  """
  Record that the responder carried the step out themselves — most often having merged the revert
  pull request a previous RUN_ACTION raised.
  """
  MARK_AS_DONE
  "Run whatever action the step publishes on actionType. The default when mode is omitted."
  RUN_ACTION
}

"The product-line classification of a knowledge source. Mirrors `MitigationSourceType`."
enum HypothesisMitigationSourceType {
  CONFLUENCE
  GOOGLE_DRIVE
  JIRA
  JSM
  MICROSOFT_SHAREPOINT
}

"The three outcomes a caller distinguishes between while polling."
enum HypothesisMitigationStateType {
  COMPLETED
  FAILED
  "Generation has been requested and has not yet reached a terminal state."
  PROGRESS
}

"How far an execution has got."
enum HypothesisMitigationStepExecutionStatus {
  """
  Stopped only because the caller's account is not linked to the provider the action needs. Distinct
  from FAILED because it is always worth retrying once the consent url published on the sub-step has
  been visited, and nothing was attempted so nothing needs undoing first.
  """
  AUTH_REQUIRED
  COMPLETED
  "Gave up: the sub-step could not be carried out."
  FAILED
  RUNNING
  "Not started yet: an earlier sub-step is still running."
  WAITING
}

"""
How a run ended, copied from JiraPlaybookStepRunStatus. Only IN_PROGRESS and SUCCESS are
reported while execution is stubbed.
"""
enum HypothesisMitigationStepRunStatus {
  ABORTED
  CONFIG_CHANGE
  FAILED
  FAILURE
  IN_PROGRESS
  LOOP
  NO_ACTIONS_PERFORMED
  QUEUED_FOR_RETRY
  SOME_ERRORS
  SUCCESS
  SUCCESS_UNDONE
  THROTTLED
  WAITING
}

"""
What a plan step does. Generated plan steps are INSTRUCTIONAL_RULE; the others arise once a user
edits the mirrored playbook.
"""
enum HypothesisMitigationStepType {
  "A step the product can carry out itself, such as reverting a pull request."
  ACTION
  AUTOMATION_RULE
  INSTRUCTIONAL_RULE
  TASK
}

