Whether `JiraAdminAgentRequestConfiguration`'s enabled set is every eligible project or a specific
curated list.
"""
enum JiraAdminAgentEnabledProjectsScope {
  """
  Every eligible project, evaluated live — not a snapshot of what was eligible when this was
  set. A project that becomes eligible after this was chosen is automatically included, with no
  further admin action.
  """
  ALL
  "Exactly the projects named in `enabledProjectIds`."
  SPECIFIC
}

"""
Why the configuration is not usable as it stands.

Domain states only — each one is a settled answer about the site, and each has a different remedy
for the administrator. Failures are not represented here: they are reported through `errors[]`,
including the transient case where the state could not be determined (see the error documented on
`jira_adminAgentRequestConfigStatus`).

No `UNKNOWN`: nothing would ever return it, and Relay already generates a `%future added value`
case for enums, which is the real forward-compatibility mechanism.
"""
enum JiraAdminAgentRequestConfigUnavailableReason {
  "A configuration exists but its destination project no longer resolves, or is archived."
  DESTINATION_INVALID
  "The feature is switched off for this site."
  FEATURE_NOT_ENABLED
  "Nothing has been configured yet. A normal first-run state, not an error."
  NOT_CONFIGURED
  "A configuration exists but its request work type no longer resolves."
  REQUEST_WORKTYPE_INVALID
}

"How much autonomy an agent has when updating a field."
enum JiraAgentAutonomyLevel {
  "The agent may update the field without user review."
  AUTO_APPLY
  """
  No autonomy level has been configured for this field. Used as a default/empty state for the
  required system fields (Description, Priority, Assignee, Labels, Due Date) when the underlying
  service returns no override for them. Entries with this level are filtered out of write requests
  before being sent to the service layer.
  """
  NOT_CONFIGURED
  "The agent must ask the user to confirm before updating the field."
  REQUIRES_APPROVAL
}

