"DRAFT / FOR REVIEW. Discriminator values for JsmChannelsProgressLogEntry.type. Only STEP_SUCCEEDED, STEP_FAILED, DECISION, HUMAN_HANDOFF, and STEP_WAITING_FOR_INPUT are confirmed against real captured runs; RUN_COMPLETED, STEP_CLARIFICATION_REQUESTED, and APPROVAL_* are documented but unconfirmed. Additive-only going forward."
enum JsmChannelsProgressLogEntryType {
  "A supervised-mode plan was approved."
  APPROVAL_GRANTED
  "A supervised-mode plan is awaiting human approval."
  APPROVAL_PENDING
  "A supervised-mode plan was rejected."
  APPROVAL_REJECTED
  "A branch decision was resolved (real multi-option branches only)."
  DECISION
  "Execution handed off to a human agent."
  HUMAN_HANDOFF
  "Customer/reporter input was received, resuming a paused conversation. Plan-level — see JsmChannelsProgressLogStepGroup.stepId."
  INPUT_RECEIVED
  "The run completed — a plan-level terminal event, not tied to any single step."
  RUN_COMPLETED
  "A step, mid-execution, requested clarification."
  STEP_CLARIFICATION_REQUESTED
  "A step failed — see summary.category for the failure bucket."
  STEP_FAILED
  "A step completed successfully."
  STEP_SUCCEEDED
  "A step's reminder retry budget was exhausted with no response received."
  STEP_TIMED_OUT
  "A step is paused, waiting for input."
  STEP_WAITING_FOR_INPUT
}

"DRAFT / FOR REVIEW. Status values for JsmChannelsProgressLogEntry.status. Deliberately its own enum, not a reuse of JsmChannelsResolutionPlanStepStatus (the real plan-step status enum, which feeds frontend rendering that isn't exhaustive over every value and would silently mislabel BLOCKED/ON_HOLD steps as 'to do')."
enum JsmChannelsProgressLogStatus {
  "Execution cannot proceed autonomously and requires a human (e.g. handoff to a human agent)."
  BLOCKED
  "Completed successfully."
  COMPLETED
  "Failed — see summary.category for the failure bucket."
  FAILED
  "Awaiting human approval before continuing (e.g. supervised-mode plan approval)."
  ON_HOLD
  "Waiting for input."
  WAITING
}

