"""
Whether the calling user can currently use a connector.

Carries no "not configured" value by design: a connector the tenant has not set up is absent from
the list entirely, which is a different statement from this user not having authorised one that
exists.
"""
enum PlaybookConnectorAuthStatus {
  """
  The user can use the connector — either they granted access themselves, or it is authorised at app
  level and they need do nothing.
  """
  CONNECTED
  """
  The connector exists for the tenant but this user has not authorised it. `consentUrl` carries where
  to send them, when one is available.
  """
  NOT_CONNECTED
  """
  The provider did not report enough to decide. Deliberately not reported as connected: presenting
  unverified access produces a failure later, where it is harder to explain. Treat it as you would
  `NOT_CONNECTED`, but do not tell the user they are disconnected.
  """
  UNKNOWN
}

