"""
Whether the PSM (SysTrack) agent is pushing data for this user's device.

NOT_REPORTING is the catch-all absence: it covers "agent installed but has never pushed
data", "agent not installed on a device we know about", and "no device registered for
this user at all". The backend cannot separate these — all three present as absent from
the provider listing — so the UI should read NOT_REPORTING as "no data flowing", not
as "installed but broken".
"""
enum PsmAgentStatus {
  "No provider reports the user's device — not installed, never started, or no device registered."
  NOT_REPORTING
  "A provider reports the user's device as online with a fresh last-seen, under the requested space."
  REPORTING
}

"Sort order. Single-field for MVP; migrate to a structured input if multi-field sort is later needed."
enum PsmAuditLogOrder {
  "Oldest first."
  TIMESTAMP_ASC
  "Newest first (default)."
  TIMESTAMP_DESC
}

"""
Outcome pill for an audit row and the values of the 'Status' filter. The remediation
statuses report whether the automation ran, NOT whether the underlying fault cleared.
Derived from the provider run: succeeded = errorCode 0 & returnCode 0; failed = a
non-zero errorCode or returnCode; not-approved = the run was declined at approval.
"""
enum PsmAuditStatus {
  "Remediation could not start, or returned a non-zero result."
  REMEDIATION_FAILED
  "Remediation was declined at the approval step, so it never ran."
  REMEDIATION_NOT_APPROVED
  "Remediation ran and returned cleanly."
  REMEDIATION_SUCCEEDED
}

"""
Relative reporting window for the audit log. Kept separate from the shared PsmTimeWindow
because the audit log also offers a 4-hour preset. CUSTOM requires filter.dateRange.
"""
enum PsmAuditTimeWindow {
  "Explicit inclusive range; requires dateRange."
  CUSTOM
  LAST_24_HOURS
  LAST_30_DAYS
  LAST_4_HOURS
  LAST_7_DAYS
}

"The employee's response to an approval prompt. Carried on CONSENT_RESPONDED events."
enum PsmConsentResponse {
  "The employee approved the remediation."
  APPROVE
  "The employee denied the remediation."
  DENY
}

"""
Read state of the conversation — a UI/notification fact, independent of remediation.
Flips from UNREAD to READ when the employee opens the conversation.
"""
enum PsmConversationReadState {
  READ
  UNREAD
}

"""
Health band a device falls into for a bucket, by health score. Same four bands as
PsmDeviceHealthStatus; not-reporting is a separate count, so it is not a band here.
"""
enum PsmDeviceHealthBand {
  "Score >= 97."
  EXCELLENT
  "Score >= 80 and < 90."
  FAIR
  "Score >= 90 and < 97."
  GOOD
  "Score < 80."
  POOR
}

"Bucket size for a trend series. Only daily buckets are produced today."
enum PsmDeviceHealthInterval {
  DAY
}

"Health band for a device, derived from provider telemetry."
enum PsmDeviceHealthStatus {
  "Device metrics are performing at optimal levels."
  EXCELLENT
  "One or more metrics are approaching threshold limits."
  FAIR
  "Device metrics are within normal thresholds."
  GOOD
  "Health data is unavailable or the device is not reporting."
  NOT_REPORTING
  "One or more metrics have breached critical thresholds."
  POOR
}

"""
The answer to a permitted poll. Every value is a settled answer the client acts on directly — a
check that could not be resolved is an error, not a status, so the client retries rather than
acting on a decision we did not actually make.
"""
enum PsmDevicePermittanceStatus {
  "Entitlement is gone (licence revoked, customer access removed, tenant downgraded). Stop PSM; do not retry."
  NOT_PERMITTED
  "No device record for this serial yet, or it was revoked. Call psm_registerDevice."
  NOT_REGISTERED
  "Keep the PSM experience running."
  PERMITTED
  "PSM is not enabled for this tenant. Stop PSM; do not retry."
  TENANT_NOT_ONBOARDED
}

"The lifecycle state of a device, derived from the shared PSM domain model."
enum PsmDeviceStatus {
  "Device is registered and reporting healthy telemetry via the provider."
  ACTIVE
  "Device is known but not currently reporting (no recent provider heartbeat)."
  OFFLINE
  "Device has a provider record but no Atlassian account binding (or vice versa)."
  ORPHAN
  "Device is registered to a tenant but not yet mapped to a provider system / space."
  UNMAPPED
}

"Whether an event was produced by the system (automation) or a named user."
enum PsmEventActor {
  SYSTEM
  USER
}

"What the client should do with the conversation after applying this event."
enum PsmEventDirective {
  "Conversation closed — move it to archive."
  ARCHIVE_CONVERSATION
  "Nothing to render for this event (e.g. transport/plumbing events)."
  NO_OP
  "Surface a new conversation (arrival)."
  SHOW_CONVERSATION
  "Patch an existing conversation in place."
  UPDATE_CONVERSATION
}

"The outcome of an automation run or attempt. Carried on EXECUTION_ATTEMPT_COMPLETED and EXECUTION_COMPLETED events."
enum PsmExecutionOutcome {
  "The automation failed (see failureReason)."
  FAILED
  "The automation was skipped (e.g. preconditions no longer met)."
  SKIPPED
  "The automation completed successfully; the issue is remediated."
  SUCCEEDED
}

"Current remediation status of a fault."
enum PsmFaultStatus {
  CLOSED
  FAILED
  OFFLINE
  OPEN
  QUEUED
}

"""
Which filter dimension this is. The same key can appear on multiple screens with a
different option set — e.g. STATUS is PsmDeviceHealthStatus values on DEVICE_LIST but
PsmSensorStatus (OPEN/CLOSED) values on ACTIVITIES.
"""
enum PsmFilterKey {
  "Device operating-system. Values are PsmOsType (WINDOWS/MAC). Present on every screen; omitted entirely when macOS support is not enabled for the tenant."
  OPERATING_SYSTEM
  "Coarse remediation grouping. Values are PsmRemediationCategory."
  REMEDIATION_CATEGORY
  "Sensor name, e.g. \"CPU Thermal Throttling\". Dynamic — sourced from configured sensors."
  SENSOR
  "Sensor/issue category, e.g. \"Hardware\", \"Network\". Dynamic — sourced from configured sensors."
  SENSOR_CATEGORY
  "Screen-specific status dimension. Values are PsmDeviceHealthStatus on DEVICE_LIST; PsmSensorStatus (OPEN/CLOSED) on ACTIVITIES; PsmAuditStatus on AUDIT_LOG."
  STATUS
  "How a remediation was triggered. Values are PsmRemediationTrigger (AUTO/AGENT/END_USER). AUDIT_LOG only."
  TRIGGERED_BY
}

"""
A screen that has a filter panel. Each maps 1:1 to a JSM PSM UI surface:
- OPEN_ISSUES_AGENT_ACTION_PENDING: Open issues screen, "Agent action pending" tab.
- OPEN_ISSUES_AUTOMATED_APPROVED: Open issues screen, "Automated & employee-approved" tab.
- DEVICE_LIST: the Devices screen.
- ACTIVITIES: the agent-facing Activities screen (past remediations).
- AUDIT_LOG: the admin-facing audit-log screen (psm_auditLog).
"""
enum PsmFilterScreen {
  ACTIVITIES
  AUDIT_LOG
  DEVICE_LIST
  OPEN_ISSUES_AGENT_ACTION_PENDING
  OPEN_ISSUES_AUTOMATED_APPROVED
}

"The IPC connection status reported for a pairing."
enum PsmIpcConnectionStatus {
  "The IPC channel for the pairing is connected."
  CONNECTED
  "The IPC channel for the pairing is disconnected."
  DISCONNECTED
  "The IPC connection status could not be determined."
  UNKNOWN
}

"The rendered shape of a message in the conversation timeline."
enum PsmMessageType {
  "Free-form markdown/text content."
  MARKDOWN
  "A ticket reference."
  TICKET
}

"Stable identifier for a notification action button, decoupled from its display label."
enum PsmNotificationActionId {
  APPROVE
  DENY
  ISSUE_RESOLVED
  RAISE_TICKET
}

"Kind of notification a template renders."
enum PsmNotificationKind {
  CONSENT_DENIED_ACK
