}

"""
Input for fetching recommended agents when re-assigning an existing covering
shift. Use `agentWorkspace_recommendedAgentsForCoverShift` instead of
`agentWorkspace_recommendedAgentsForCoverageGap` when the covering shift
already exists — the service will look up the original agent internally so
they are never blocked from the recommended set.

Uses the same addressing key as `AgentWorkspaceEditCoverShiftInput` so the FE
can reuse the values it already has when opening the agent picker.
"""
input AgentWorkspaceRecommendedAgentsForCoverShiftInput {
  """
  The agent currently assigned to the covering shift, sourced from
  `AgentWorkspaceCoveringShift.coveringAgentId`.
  """
  agentId: ID!
  coveringShiftId: ID!
  """
  Start time of the occurrence this covering shift belongs to, sourced from
  `AgentWorkspaceCoveringShift.occurrenceStartTime`.
  """
  occurrenceStartTime: DateTime!
  projectARI: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "project", usesActivationId : false)
  scheduleId: ID!
}

"""
Input for `agentWorkspace_recommendedAgentsForCoverageGap`. Addresses the
gap by `scheduleId` (the only stable id today) plus `gapOwnerAgentId` (the
rostered/root agent for the occurrence the gap derives from). The gap owner
is always allowed back into the recommended set even when they are listed
on the schedule. Per-gap-window narrowing (`occurrenceStartTime`,
`gapStartTime`, `gapEndTime`) will be added when the reader rewrite needs
it (REQIN-4619b). Successor to `AgentWorkspaceRecommendedAgentsForGapInput`.
"""
input AgentWorkspaceRecommendedAgentsForCoverageGapInput {
  """
  The rostered (root) agent for the schedule occurrence the gap derives
  from — i.e. the agent who would otherwise have worked the shift. This
  agent is always recommended (never excluded) even if they appear on the
  schedule.
  """
  gapOwnerAgentId: ID!
  projectARI: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "project", usesActivationId : false)
  """
  The schedule the gap belongs to, sourced from
  `AgentWorkspaceCoverageGap.scheduleId`.
  """
  scheduleId: ID!
}

