"""
Input for allocating one or more contributors to a single work item.
This mutation is scope-free so that MCP and other non-UI consumers do not need a board or
scope ID. Each contributor is assigned to the work item (idempotent) and every allocation
is upserted for every contributor.

The number of contributors multiplied by the number of allocations must not exceed 100,
which is the bulk limit on the underlying contribution write.
"""
input CplsAllocateCapacityInput {
  """
  The allocations to apply to every contributor. Periods must be distinct; an existing
  allocation for the same contributor, work item and exact period is replaced. Neither a
  single period nor the window spanning all of them may exceed two years.
  """
  allocations: [CplsAllocationInput!]!
  cloudId: ID! @CloudID(owner : "jira")
  "The contributors to allocate to the work item."
  contributorDataIds: [ID!]! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "identity", type : "user", usesActivationId : false)
  """
  The work item to allocate to: a Jira work item, Atlas project, or non-project work
  item (custom contribution target) ARI.
  """
  workId: ID!
}

"""
A single allocation period and its value. Mirrors CplsAddContributionInput, without the
contributor and work item, which are supplied once on CplsAllocateCapacityInput.

The period may be any length up to two years: one week, one month, a single day, or a whole
quarter. The value is the total for that period, so express a rate by supplying one entry per
period (three days per week for September is five entries of three days, not one of three).
"""
input CplsAllocationInput {
  "End of the allocation period. Must not be more than two years after startDate."
  endDate: Date!
  "Start of the allocation period. Must not be after endDate."
  startDate: Date!
  "Allocation value in the given unit. Must be >= 0; zero clears the allocation."
  value: Float!
  "Unit of the allocation value."
  valueType: CplsContributionValueType!
}

input CplsCapacityPlanSettingsInput {
  fortnightAnchorDate: Date
  weekStartDay: CplsDayOfWeek
}

"""
Date range for the nested contribution cells. It does not affect which contributor-work
associations are returned. One-sided inputs are completed to a two-year range; omitting both
dates uses a window from one year before today to one year after today. Supplying both dates
requires an ordered range of at most two years.
"""
input CplsContributionDateRange {
  endDate: Date
  startDate: Date
}

"A single contributor work association entry."
input CplsContributorWorkAssociation {
