  containerUrl: URL!
  isCodeReviewerEnabled: Boolean!
  triggerMode: DevAiCodeReviewerTriggerMode!
  type: DevAiScmAdminContainerType!
}

"""
Sets `triggerMode` on the repositories the user administers on the provider that have Code Reviewer on with a manual
trigger, in a workspace that has it on too. Nothing is turned on. A GitHub org that's on but not linked to a site is
linked to this one when the user is its admin or a Jira admin, and its repositories are changed. Repositories with their
own settings are left as they were. The others follow the defaults, so they're only changed when those turn Code
Reviewer on with a manual trigger.
"""
input DevAiScmAdminCodeReviewerProviderSettingInput {
  "Only `true` is supported for now."
  isCodeReviewerEnabled: Boolean!
  provider: DevAiScmAdminProvider!
  triggerMode: DevAiCodeReviewerTriggerMode!
}

"Send `providers`, `containers` or both. An item in `containers` takes precedence over its provider."
input DevAiScmAdminCodeReviewerSettingsInput {
  "`endCursor` from the previous call, to continue after `hasMore`."
  after: String
  "Specific workspaces or repositories, at most 100. Saved exactly as sent, on the first call only."
  containers: [DevAiScmAdminCodeReviewerContainerSettingInput!]
  "Everything the user administers on each provider. Each provider can be listed once."
  providers: [DevAiScmAdminCodeReviewerProviderSettingInput!]
}

