"Input for `playbook_executeHypothesisMitigationStep`."
input ExecuteHypothesisMitigationStepInput {
  """
  Ignored — do not send. Which action a step runs is decided when its plan is built from the
  hypothesis and stored on the plan, and is published on HypothesisMitigationPlanStep.actionType.
  Retained only so a client still sending it does not fail schema validation, and will be removed
  once none does. To mark a step done instead of running its action, use `mode`.
  
  
  This field is **deprecated** and will be removed in the future
  """
  actionType: HypothesisMitigationActionType
  """
  Whether to run the step's action or record that the responder did it themselves. Omit it to run
  the action, which is what every caller did before marking done existed.
  """
  mode: HypothesisMitigationExecutionMode
  """
  ARI of the playbook instance step, as published on HypothesisMitigationPlanStep.stepId. The
  server resolves the step from it and reads what to do, and what to do it to, off the plan behind
  it.
  """
  stepId: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook-instance-step", usesActivationId : false)
}

