"Inputs for updating an existing MCP server registration"
input GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementUpdateMcpRegistrationInput @renamed(from : "McpAdminManagementUpdateMcpRegistrationInput") {
  """
  The access mode to apply to the MCP server. Only supported for servers whose access is governed by
  RBAC — API_TOKEN or CUSTOM_OAUTH_CLIENT_CREDENTIALS — and the request is rejected if it is supplied
  for any other auth type. If not provided, the access mode is left unchanged.
  """
  accessMode: GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementMcpServerAccessMode
  """
  The auth configuration to apply to the MCP server. When provided with an apiToken variant, rotates the stored
  API token for a server already registered with API_TOKEN authentication. If not provided, auth is left unchanged.
  """
  authConfig: GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementMcpServerAuthConfigInput
  "Whether newly discovered tools should be automatically enabled after a tool sync. If not provided, the value will not be updated."
  autoEnableNewTools: Boolean
  "The cloudId where the operation is being performed."
  cloudId: ID! @CloudID
  "The ARI of the MCP server to update."
  serverId: ID!
}

"""
Identifies the MCP server whose custom auth configuration is being updated, and the values to apply.

Takes the same auth config input the registration mutation takes, so the registration form's auth
component emits one payload shape for both flows.
"""
input GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementUpdateMcpServerAuthConfigInput @renamed(from : "McpAdminManagementUpdateMcpServerAuthConfigInput") {
  """
  The values to apply. Template values that are omitted keep the value currently in force, so an
  edit form only has to submit what it rendered.
  
  The client secret is the exception: it must be supplied on every edit whenever the provider
  requires one, because it cannot be read back and the provider configuration is replaced rather
  than patched. Omitting it is rejected rather than silently clearing it.
  
  The authType must match the server's current one: switching auth type is not supported here.
  """
  authConfig: GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementMcpServerAuthConfigInput!
  "The site the MCP server is registered in."
  cloudId: ID!
  "The ARI of the MCP server whose custom auth configuration should be updated."
  serverId: ID!
}

"Inputs for updating the configuration of one or more MCP tools"
input GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementUpdateMcpToolConfigurationInput @renamed(from : "McpAdminManagementUpdateMcpToolConfigurationInput") {
  "The cloudId where the operation is being performed."
  cloudId: ID! @CloudID
  "The ARI of the MCP server where the tools are configured."
  serverId: ID!
  "A list of MCP tool configurations to update."
  toolConfigurations: [GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementMcpToolConfigurationInput!]!
}

