"""
Input for the `marketplaceStore.siteInfo` query.

Returns a SINGLE enriched site description for the calling user. Both
inputs are optional; their combination drives one of four execution modes.

Modes A–C below describe the path when feature gate
`enable_all_parameter_site_info` is ON. When OFF, Modes A–C use the
legacy userbase-/org-shard RBP discovery (pre-org-scoped) behaviour.

  - `cloudId + orgId` (both supplied) — Mode A:
        TCS confirms the cloudId belongs to the supplied orgId. Then one
        Identity RBP call with `scopeId=<org ARI>`, `all=true`, and an
        exact site `resourceFilter` (`arm:cloud:.+::site/{cloudId}`).
        Org mismatch, TCS failure, Identity failure, or no canonical
        product grants → `{ site: null }` (no existence leak).

  - `cloudId` only — Mode B:
        Derive org via TCS `getOrgId(cloudId)`, then the same org-scoped
        exact-site RBP path as Mode A. Miss → `{ site: null }`.

  - `orgId` only — Mode C:
        One org-scoped RBP (`scopeId=<org ARI>`, `all=true`,
        `arm:cloud:.+::site/.+`). Candidates are TCS-verified against
        `orgId` (mandatory: invalid/unknown org scope can return
        unscoped results). First verified site wins (stable: sorted
        cloudId). Miss → `{ site: null }`.

  - neither supplied — Mode D:
        Discovery fans out across the user's userbases; the first
        userbase that returns ANY site wins. Which site arrives first
        is NOT deterministic across requests. Callers needing a stable
        "first site" must always pass `cloudId`.

When a targeted mode (A/B/C) misses and `returnDefault` is true, the resolver
falls back to Mode-D-style first accessible site.

Validation: both inputs accept any alphanumeric + hyphen + underscore string
up to 80 chars. Whitespace, control characters or other special characters
return `BAD_USER_INPUT`.
"""
input MarketplaceStoreSiteInfoInput {
  """
  Optional. If supplied, the resolver tries to return THIS specific site.
  When access cannot be confirmed, `site` is null.
  """
  cloudId: String
  """
  Optional. When supplied with `cloudId`, both must match (Mode A).
  When supplied alone, selects one site in this org via org-scoped RBP
  plus TCS verification (Mode C).
  """
  orgId: String
  """
  Optional. When true and a targeted lookup (cloudId and/or orgId) resolves to
  no accessible site, fall back to returning the caller's first available site
  instead of null. No-op when neither cloudId nor orgId is supplied (that case
  already returns the first site).
  """
  returnDefault: Boolean
}

"appKey and parentProduct for the app for which information to be fetched"
input MarketplaceStoreSiteProduct {
  appKey: String
  parentProduct: MarketplaceStoreInstallationTargetProduct
}

