  notifyOnReviewResponseOrUpdate: Boolean!
}

"""
Input for the `marketplaceStore.userSites` query.

Filtering: when `productFilter` is null/empty/omitted the resolver runs in
STORE mode and returns every site the user has access to. When non-empty it
runs in EMCEE mode and drops sites whose intersected `products[]` (Identity
RBP grants ∩ `MarketplaceStoreTransformer.activeProducts`) has no overlap
with the requested products — a site with a stale Confluence permission but
no longer-active Confluence license is dropped. A pre-filter is also applied
at dedupe time on the raw RBP grants to bound enrichment workload; the strict
correctness filter runs AFTER enrichment so that only truly-usable products
satisfy the filter.

Pagination is performed entirely BFF-side because Identity's
`/v4/permissions/resourcesByPrincipalPermissions` does NOT honour any
page-size parameter (`limit`, `pageSize`, `maxResults`, `size` are all
silently ignored — verified by live probe on 2026-05-20). The full deduped
site list is sorted ascending by `cloudId`; the page is produced by
binary-searching the cursor into that array. There is no local caching —
every request re-runs the discovery pipeline.
"""
input MarketplaceStoreUserSitesInput {
  """
  Caller surface. When omitted, the resolver derives it from request shape
  (STORE if no product filter, EMCEE otherwise). Pass explicitly when the
  derivation heuristic is wrong (e.g. STORE callers filtering by product).
  """
  context: MarketplaceStoreUserSitesContext
  """
  Opaque cursor; equals the bare `cloudId` of the LAST site returned in the
  previous page (no base64). The resolver uses binary search to find the next
  slice. When omitted, the first page is returned. Cursors that do not match
  any site in the current list are treated as the start of the list.
  """
  cursor: String
  """
  Maximum number of sites to return per page.
  
  ENFORCED BY THE RESOLVER (not by the GraphQL schema):
    - Default when null/omitted: 20
    - Hard floor: 1
    - Hard ceiling: 100
  
  Out-of-range values are clamped silently rather than rejected so that
  client-side cursor recovery (e.g. URL deep-link with stale `limit`) cannot
  break the page.
  """
  limit: Int
  """
  Optional product filter (EMCEE mode). When omitted/null/empty the resolver
  returns sites matching ALL supported products.
  """
  productFilter: [MarketplaceStoreProductType!]
}

